# 2026-03-03 20:42:05.443070
+Review this Go codebase (iotex-core) for:
+
+  1. **Security vulnerabilities**: buffer overflows, integer overflows, unchecked error
+   returns, SQL/command injection, unsafe deserialization, race conditions, missing
+  mutex locks on shared state, private key handling issues.
+
+  2. **Concurrency bugs**: goroutine leaks (missing context cancellation, unbounded
+  goroutine spawning), deadlocks (lock ordering violations, channel misuse), data races
+   on maps/slices without sync.
+
+  3. **Error handling**: swallowed errors (err assigned but not checked), panics in
+  production paths, missing nil checks on interface returns, defer Close() without
+  error check.
+
+  4. **Performance**: O(n^2) loops on large datasets, excessive allocations in hot
+  paths, missing connection pooling, unbounded caches/maps that grow forever.
+
+  5. **Logic bugs**: off-by-one in slice/array indexing, incorrect type assertions
+  without ok check, fallthrough in switch cases, wrong comparison operators.
+
+  For each finding, output:
+  - File path and line number
+  - Severity: CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW
+  - Category (from above)
+  - Description of the issue
+  - Suggested fix (code snippet)
+
+  Focus on the most impactful issues first. Skip cosmetic/style issues entirely.

